<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caratacus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Caractacus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Caratacus was a British chieftain, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cunobelinus">Cunobelinus</a> of the Catuvellauni, who led resistance to the Roman invasion of 43 CE. After the fall of his homeland he continued the war among the Silures and Ordovices of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, until he was defeated around 50. He fled to the Brigantes, whose queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cartimandua">Cartimandua</a> handed him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a> spared his life.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caratacus.jpg" alt="Caratacus" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CaractacusClaudius.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
